{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789774105,"nonce":"/H6df91Pxlzhs9YG5fd7TcBJxxE=","title":"Std.string / concat / Sys.println disagree on Dynamic boxes, enums and class instances","message":"Probes (/tmp/probe/p9217/C1.hx, T1-T4.hx):\n- `var k:Dynamic = Reflect.field(o, \"kid\"); \"\" + k.v` printed the box's\n  payload pointer (12885950528) and `k.s` crashed: the Let took the\n  `Ptr(U8)` result of a Dynamic-returning stdlib call for a RAW anonymous\n  handle (`raw_anon_symbols`), so `k.v` went through `haxe_reflect_field`\n  (raw-object entry) instead of the tag-aware `haxe_dynamic_field`, and the\n  class box's `value_ptr` was read as field 1.\n- `Sys.println(1.5)` printed nothing and the run ended; `Sys.println(Red)`,\n  `Sys.println([1,2])`, `Sys.println(obj)` passed the raw value to\n  `haxe_string_println` as if it were a HaxeString. Only Int survived\n  because the runtime tolerates an Int box.\n- `\"\" + Red` / `Std.string(Green(3))` printed the enum's address: an enum\n  is an i64 in MIR and the stringifier had no Enum arm (`int_to_string`).\n- `Std.string(d)` for a class instance held as Dynamic printed \"void\":\n  every registered class has `to_string: void_to_string`; the runtime had\n  no way to reach a Haxe `toString`.\n- `Reflect.field(o, nullIntField) == null` was false (the slot's box\n  pointer/null was boxed again as Int) and `Type.typeof(arrayBox)` was\n  TUnknown.\n\nFix: a resolved stdlib static call declared to return Dynamic marks its\nresult as a box (`note_dynamic_stdlib_result`); print/println stringify a\nnon-String argument the way Std.string does; `convert_to_string_with_hint`\ngains an Enum arm over new `haxe_enum_to_string[_boxed]` (sharing the\ntrace formatter; String params print unquoted as Haxe does);\n`__vtable_init__` registers each user class's `toString` code pointer\n(`haxe_type_register_to_string`) and `haxe_std_string_ptr` calls it for a\nclass-tagged box, else prints the class name; `IrFieldShape::Boxed` /\n`ParamType::Boxed` hands a `Null\u003cscalar\u003e` slot back as it is; TYPE_ARRAY\nis TClass.\n\nLeft out: stdlib classes' `toString` (Exception, StringBuf, List...) are\nNOT registered — a `fn_ref` from a stdlib module's `__vtable_init__` keeps\nthe method's callees live, and the selective import merge left\n`haxe.Int64.copy` as a body-less stub in the user module (\"can't resolve\nsymbol copy\" at Cranelift finalize). Filed separately.","files":null}]}